00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.710 align:start position:0%
as they do every December European  fisheries ministers will try to clinch  agreement on fishing opportunities for  next year for certain stocks in EU and  some non EU waters at their Council in  Brussels this annual process is based on  recommendations from the European  Commission taking into account  scientific advice it concerns stocks in  the Atlantic the North Sea International  fishing where EU vessels take part and  in the black sea fishing opportunity  limits are aimed at keeping stocks  sustainable they take the form of total  allowable catches or tax for each stock  and each fishing zone tax are then  divided into quotas between member  states the Commission will also brief  ministers on the way the fishing landing  obligation is being implemented the  rules are part of recent reform to the  common fishing policy and will enter  force in January to ensure that less  fish are thrown away meanwhile the  Italian presidency will report to  agriculture ministers on progress  achieved during the second half of this  year on the legislative proposals like a  review of organic farming legislation  the school fruit vegetable and milk  scheme official controls and plant  health they'll also exchanged views on  the future of the dairy sector notably  on price volatility in the market and  ways to limit the impact of the Russian  banner Europe on dairy produce the  Commission for its part will present the  main sections of its simplification  agenda for farm policy it aimed at  keeping down costs to farmers and other  operators in the sector
 

